# Innocent Blood and a creature under another player's control: a player sacrifices a creature they control (CR 701.21a), and a
# permanent that leaves goes to its owner's graveyard (CR 400.3). Bot1 steals Bot2's only creature (Llanowar Elves) with
# Vengeful Possession, so Bot1 controls two creatures and Bot2 none. Bot1 chooses the stolen Elves (not the Ornithopter that was
# offered first): it goes to Bot2's graveyard, its owner's, Bot2 has nothing of its own to sacrifice, and Bot1 keeps Ornithopter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Vengeful Possession
Innocent Blood
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vengeful Possession.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Innocent Blood.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Innocent Blood; Vengeful Possession
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
